.1--plan/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r8.1--plan","local_name":"sase-1r8.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1r8","agent_clan_generation":"20261104135618","agent_session":"sase-1r8.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"sase-1r8.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1r8[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Stop agent publication false blocks, parked-row floods, and drain [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]starvation[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The background agent_publication job stops reporting scanner false [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]positives every pass. bob-cli's stuck and starved rows publish. A [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]request withheld by publication protection can no longer starve its[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]project or flood the error digest. A future scanner-rule correction[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]releases its own stale false blocks with provenance, and .land [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]coder rows stop quarantining over a prompt archive that already [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]exists.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]agent_publication_errors.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/agent_publication_errors.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1r8[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1r8/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Anchor the scanner rules and make scanner-hit blocks [/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]rules-versioned (sase-core)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: in sase-core, add a left token boundary to the prefix credential [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rules, bump the scanner rules version to 2, make a scanner-hit block [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]enforced only while its evidence is current, supersede stale blocks with[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]provenance on a clean rescan, add a parked-recheck predicate, and expose[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]all of it through bindings with tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One drain loop that never lets a failing row starve its [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]project[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]drain[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]drain: replace the hinted-then-fallback loops in publication_job with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one loop that excludes keys already attempted this pass, stops only on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repository-scope failures, reports failure scope on the drain outcome, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and compacts claimed hint files to at most one per project.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Recognize a session member's prompt archive for .land coder [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]rows[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]land_prompt[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]land_prompt: make the deferred-restore archive check accept an archive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whose AGENTS label is a member of the request's own agent session (for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]example the --plan member), indexed once per restore call, so .land [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]coder rows acknowledge instead of quarantining.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Consume the rules-versioned protection policy in sase[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]protection[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]protection: move the sase-core pin, route every ledger lookup through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the enforced-lookup binding so stale blocks are rescanned, pass the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]clean rules version into resolve so stale blocks are superseded, keep [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]superseded history on disk, and teach doctor to separate enforced, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stale, and superseded records.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Park protection-withheld requests instead of retrying them [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]every pass[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]parking[dim] · [dim][/dim]after drain, protection[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]parking: add parked fields to the outbox (schema 8), park withheld and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt-protection rows at settlement, keep parked rows out of selection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the self-ring until the Rust recheck predicate says they are due, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stop counting parks as job errors (except per park_notice), and surface [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parked counts in the heartbeat, chop summary, and doctor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Install, verify live on athena, and hand off follow-ups[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after land_prompt, parking[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify: propose the human-only reinstall through a gate if the installed[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]build predates the fix, then confirm on athena that bob-cli's stuck and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]starved rows drain, claim files compact, stale blocks are superseded, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the d